{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-351304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{a}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{a} \\\\  & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})) \\\\  & =8\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/28afd0a065525cd225377165c2164a1ecc254b1be8aba60d64324d14430c3be4.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-351304" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351304" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8\\pi}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{8}{1+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(z)+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{8}{1+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}\\frac{1}{1+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(z)]_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)] \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{4}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)])\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/27ec65761e5119be666e69b67b2fa2fcb7b4f3665ddc41faddd6c136d5c955b1.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{8}{1+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{4}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)]) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-152090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "4\\pi "] ["math" "8\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{10}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{10}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)]_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)] \\\\  & =10\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)]-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/27ec65761e5119be666e69b67b2fa2fcb7b4f3665ddc41faddd6c136d5c955b1.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{10}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)]-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =10\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-152081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\pi "] ["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "5\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{1+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(z)+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{1+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{a}\\frac{1}{1+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(z)]_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{a} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})] \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})] \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)]+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/27ec65761e5119be666e69b67b2fa2fcb7b4f3665ddc41faddd6c136d5c955b1.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{1+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =4\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)]+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-152083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "4\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{10\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{10\\pi }{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{a}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,{|}_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{a} \\\\  & =12\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})) \\\\  & =12\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =12\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/28afd0a065525cd225377165c2164a1ecc254b1be8aba60d64324d14430c3be4.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =10\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-351303" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351303" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+(kx)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(kx)+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{1}{1+16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{1}{1+(4x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4a)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/4daa526482964d826d5cf17a9a646de0a01059e7f886ddd1e19bcb09c4c25ee3.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4a) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-351307" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351307" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-347131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/2}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{4{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-347131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+(kx)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(kx)+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{4{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =18\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1/2}^{a}\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =18\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1/2}^{a}\\frac{1}{(2x)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =18\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)]}_{1/2}^{a} \\\\  & =9\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =9\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/2ad762128a32c119f1783b88b4d10ae6820a914689296f03eedad206e097a29d.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{4{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =9\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)-\\frac{9\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{9\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-347131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-347131" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-347131" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9\\pi}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1/(2\\sqrt{3})}\\frac{6}{1+36{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+(kx)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(kx)+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1/(2\\sqrt{3})}\\frac{6}{1+36{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1/(2\\sqrt{3})}\\frac{1}{1+36{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1/(2\\sqrt{3})}\\frac{1}{1+(6x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)]}_{a}^{1/(2\\sqrt{3})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6a)] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6a)].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/faa31c8261818c5c978d984a9b90a13e58794b02ff6f47e868ad6d5a06b7f71a.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1/(2\\sqrt{3})}\\frac{6}{1+36{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6a)] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-152121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{6}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+(kx)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(kx)+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{6}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{1+(2x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)]}_{a}^{-\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)] \\\\  & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)) \\\\  & =-\\pi -3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/382ca84f05af04af9c9b2c837d549a09b695574781f12bc67b8438b95b5f5d75.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\pi -3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)] \\\\  & =-\\pi -3\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\pi +\\frac{3\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-152124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-347129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/9}^{\\infty }\\frac{15}{9{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-347129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+(kx)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(kx)+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/9}^{\\infty }\\frac{15}{9{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =15\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/9}^{a}\\frac{1}{9{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/9}^{a}\\frac{1}{(3x)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =15\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)]}_{\\sqrt{3}/9}^{a} \\\\  & =5\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3a)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})) \\\\  & =5\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3a)-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3a)-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/9f882cb5102270dfe4bef256782c18aaeeca3518f564cd188298040237e30f62.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/9}^{\\infty }\\frac{15}{9{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3a)-\\frac{5\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{5\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-347129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-347129" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-347129" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{k}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{k})+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{2})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{2})]-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/042ad2450306552d9d5a7e4219d15547ad7104601b7ce6350a64193981de0de7.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{2})]-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-152128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\pi "] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-152128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-6037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-6037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{k}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{k})+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{z}{3})]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/2465f099a94aa966dbf33eb89aa00973e692fa97c887a9b79baff8260f5d31cd.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-6037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-6037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-6037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-6037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{6}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{k}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{k})+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{6}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{z}{3})]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (0-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/a4961fa6f4f1aafeba2e8f77ed91e7d034fffd6aa249f13bb8357da11a7cea5e.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{6}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z & =2\\cdot (0-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (0-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d5a10153ce4677e9cadafa6ee5775de78829474fdca6d284f7beccb72de596d"} {"question" "q-351568" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-351568" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-119199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}u=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/state.json" "file_sha256" "f80f97e6d5da3d47fd38719f271772f3751a91191b1cd1f18702857ef5ae34ba"} {"question" "q-119199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{k}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{k})+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}u & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{u}{\\sqrt{3}})]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{3}})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{3}})] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6\\sqrt{3}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{3}})].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/11c74897fe914599a78c5997767bad83d13ddfb1e35ee66622d8880743688bad.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{\\pi }{6\\sqrt{3}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{3}})] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6\\sqrt{3}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer